Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:57:11 -0700
Subject: Printing: Upgrade a DCHECK() in PrintRenderFrameHelper

A sample CDP driver can trigger a DCHECK() failure in
PrintRenderFrameHelper::GetPrintManagerHost(). Upgrade it to a CHECK()
so the renderer crashes instead of doing something worse.

Bug: 574409275
Change-Id: I1cad28c41e5e006a462578820b5b35969652bc43
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8638189
Commit-Queue: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Peter Kvitek <kvitekp@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1726016}

diff --git a/components/printing/renderer/print_render_frame_helper.cc b/components/printing/renderer/print_render_frame_helper.cc
index 4532fbdb7735764caf2eb472c94a3f756d55b790..3bd4e07f33d0d463695793ab1f125a050f51aacc 100644
--- a/components/printing/renderer/print_render_frame_helper.cc
+++ b/components/printing/renderer/print_render_frame_helper.cc
@@ -1163,7 +1163,7 @@ PrintRenderFrameHelper::~PrintRenderFrameHelper() = default;
 const mojo::AssociatedRemote<mojom::PrintManagerHost>&
 PrintRenderFrameHelper::GetPrintManagerHost() {
   // We should not make calls back to the host while handling PrintWithParams().
-  DCHECK(!print_with_params_callback_);
+  CHECK(!print_with_params_callback_);
 
   if (!print_manager_host_) {
